  "dom_id": "step-q328221",
  "name": "Question 4",
  "problem": "A  linear transformation $T$ represents a dilation. Given that $v=[\\begin{aligned}-1 \\\\ 4\\end{aligned}]$ and $T(v)=[\\begin{aligned}-5 \\\\ 20\\end{aligned}],$ what is the standard matrix $T$ of $T?$\n\n| $T=\\,\\,$ |  | {{field-1}} | {{field-2}} |  |\n| --- | --- | --- | --- | --- |\n|  | {{field-3}} | {{field-4}} |  |  |",
  "worked_solution": "We can write $T(v)$ as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}T(v) & =[\\begin{aligned}-5 \\\\ 20\\end{aligned}] \\\\  & =5\\cdot [\\begin{aligned}-1 \\\\ 4\\end{aligned}] \\\\  & =5v\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSo we have $T(v)=5v,$ and so the linear transformation $T$ is a dilation with scale factor $k=5.$\n\nThe matrix that represents a dilation of scale factor $k$ is given by\n\n$$\n[\\begin{aligned}k & 0 \\\\ 0 & k\\end{aligned}].\n$$\n\nTherefore, the standard matrix of $T$ is\n\n$$\nT=[\\begin{aligned}5 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 5\\end{aligned}].\n$$",
